<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese three-month car sales fall 4.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Portuguese three-month car sales fall 4.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese Auto-Dealers Association (ACAP) announced the following new car registrations:</p>
<p>March     1997 22,175 vs 22,849 (down 2.9 pct)</p>
<p>Jan-March 1997 55,648 vs 57,982 (down 4.0 pct)</p>
<p>First three months by manufacturers' market share (percentage in brackets). Comparative figures refer to same period in 1996:</p>
<p>    Fiat	 8,153 (14.65) vs 8,995 (15.51)</p>
<p>    Opel	   8,111 (14.58) vs 8,508 (14.67)</p>
<p>    Renault   7,166 (12.88) vs 7,923 (13.66)</p>
<p>    Ford	    5,883 (10.57) vs 6.081 (10.49)</p>
<p>    Volkswagen 4,679  (8.41) vs 4,500  (7.76)</p>
<p>    Citroen   3,880  (6.97) vs 2,819  (4.86)</p>
<p>    Peugeot   2,999  (5.39) vs 3,930  (6.78)</p>
<p>    Honda	1,974  (3.55) vs 2,215  (3.82)</p>
<p>    Seat	 1,648  (2.96) vs 1,933  (3.33)</p>
<p>    Nissan     1,213  (2.18) vs 1,340  (2.31)</p>
</text>
